# Protocol Synapsix — Cursor Rules

## Naming conventions
- Database columns: snake_case
- Dart/TypeScript variables & functions: camelCase
- Classes, widgets, React components: PascalCase

## Folder structure (do not deviate)
mobile/lib/features/<feature>/{data,domain,presentation}/ — Clean Architecture split:
  data = I/O (sensors, storage, network), domain = pure logic/models (unit-testable),
  presentation = widgets/screens.
backend/app/{api,core,services,schemas}/
dashboard/src/{pages,components,hooks,lib,types}/

## Runtime agent placeholders — IMPORTANT
The five runtime "agents" (SensorIngestionAgent, MotionClassifierAgent, LearnedOdometryAgent,
FusionAgent/EKF, MapMatchingAgent) are PLACEHOLDER-ONLY. Do not implement real Kalman
filtering, real TFLite inference, or real HMM map-matching unless explicitly told to.
Every file for these must keep its `// TODO(agentic-workflow): replace with real
implementation` comment at the top. The real implementations will be supplied separately —
your job is only to keep the interfaces/shapes correct so they're a drop-in replacement later.

## General
- Every network/sensor call: wrapped in try/catch, typed error surfaced to UI. No silent failures.
- Preserve existing inline comments when editing files — never strip them.
- Never write real API keys into any file. Only `.env.example` with placeholder values.